**Construction 17.2 (one-Tick scout and constant-grid assay).** Execute
one actual Tick and Hold, including when $n=0$. At the first earned
terminal, request digital precisions $1,2,4,\ldots$, without changing
the field, until the first complete report $k_*\ge2$. Let $p_*$ be
its precision and $d$ the number of scout Reads. Compute integers

$$
L=6p_*,\qquad M=3(L+n),\qquad P=M+1.
\tag{17.1}
$$

At that same held epoch Read all $b$ terminals at precision $P$.
For $r=1,\ldots,n$, execute one actual Tick, Hold, and all $b$ Reads
at the same precision $P$. Retain each actual integer $k_{r,j}$ and
extract

$$
Y_{r,j}=2^{-M}\left\lfloor k_{r,j}/2\right\rfloor.
\tag{17.2}
$$

Every input, integer response, provider bit, arithmetic operand and
complete lifecycle has the actual backing of §§7–8. The scout Hold is
also the epoch-zero Hold; no second epoch-zero Hold is inserted.

